On Jul 22, 2008, at 5:38 , Dave DeCaprio wrote:

> I’m using jgr on windows.  Is there are option to set the memory  
> parameters for the JVM differently.  Right now it defaults to 64Mb  
> and I need more than that.
>

You can simply set -Xmx512m or whichever amount you need (see java -X  
for details).

I have modified the launcher to increase the default to 512MB (which  
is the default on all other platforms). The new launcher also now  
supports --libpath=xx and --rhome=xx directives for those that may  
find this useful (i.e. those with non-standard library paths). The  
code is currently in the SVN, but I hope it will be released on the  
webpage as well.

Cheers,
Simon



